<title>USA: Shell Oil seen fixing new California coker.</title>
<headline>Shell Oil seen fixing new California coker.</headline>
<dateline>MARTINEZ, Calif. 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Operators of a new coker at Shell Oil Co's 146,000 barrel-per-day refinery in Martinez, California, have fixed the unit's start-up problems and brought it on line , said a source familiar with the plant.</p>
<p>&quot;There were some pump problems but they have been resolved,&quot; said the industry source.</p>
<p>The new $1 billion coker converts heavy, low-grade oils into light products.</p>
<p>Shell Oil is a unit of the Anglo-Dutch oil giant Royal Dutch/Shell Group.</p>
<p>A refinery spokeswoman was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Brinkerhoff, Los Angeles Bureau +1 213 380 2014</p>
